@page "/demos/overflow-navigation"
<PageTitle>Overflow navigation — Lily Blazor examples</PageTitle>

@*
    Overflow navigation demo (plan P18-T3), the Blazor port of the SvelteKit
    route /demos/overflow-navigation. Renders the real NavigationMenu with
    Overflow, so its collocated JS module (NavigationMenu.razor.js, loaded
    through JS interop after the first interactive render) measures the list
    in a browser. e2e/overflow-navigation.spec.ts checks it at 1200, 420 and
    320 CSS pixels, and with JavaScript disabled (the prerendered HTML: the
    links wrap and the More item stays hidden).

    The paragraph after the navigation is the "content below": opening the
    More list must push it down (normal flow), never cover it (WCAG 2.4.11).
    The items are fixed: the module moves them in the DOM behind Blazor's
    back, so they must not change while the component is rendered.
*@

<h1>Overflow navigation</h1>
<p>
    The navigation menu below is in overflow mode: the links that do not fit on one row move
    into a "More" list. Without JavaScript the links wrap.
</p>

<NavigationMenu Label="Main navigation" Overflow="true" MoreLabel="More" data-testid="overflow-nav">
    @foreach (var item in Items)
    {
        <li><a href="@item.Href" aria-current="@(item.Current ? "page" : null)">@item.Text</a></li>
    }
</NavigationMenu>

<p data-testid="content-below">
    This paragraph follows the navigation. Opening the More list pushes it down.
</p>

@code {
    private sealed record NavItem(string Href, string Text, bool Current = false);

    private static readonly NavItem[] Items =
    [
        new("#home", "Home", true),
        new("#appointments", "Appointments"),
        new("#prescriptions", "Prescriptions"),
        new("#test-results", "Test results"),
        new("#messages", "Messages"),
        new("#health-record", "Health record"),
        new("#settings", "Settings"),
        new("#help", "Help"),
    ];
}
